# Android build workflow

- **Default:** Build APKs **locally** with the Android SDK (not EAS).
- **When to rebuild:** new/changed native module (clipboard, location, speech, audio, haptics, …), or a `versionCode` bump. JS-only → Metro reload.
- **Versioning:** `npm run release -- <major|minor|patch|x.y.z>` — never hand-edit `expo.version` / `expo.android.versionCode` in `app.json`, `package.json`, or the lockfile. The script bumps `versionCode` and syncs all three; a test fails if they drift. **Then run `npx expo prebuild --platform android`** — gradle reads the version from `android/app/build.gradle`, so without prebuild the APK ships the old `versionCode`.

## Packages (side-by-side)

| Build | Package | Label | Use |
|-------|---------|-------|-----|
| **Debug** | `com.lifeapp.dashboard.dev` | **dev** | Coding + Metro |
| **Release** | `com.lifeapp.dashboard` | **prod** | Standalone (JS embedded) |

Debug uses `applicationIdSuffix '.dev'` and `resValue "string", "app_name", "dev"`. Do **not** install debug over a differently signed release package.

## Local build

```bash
export ANDROID_HOME="$HOME/Android/Sdk"
export ANDROID_SDK_ROOT="$ANDROID_HOME"
export JAVA_HOME="$HOME/.local/jdk-21"   # if set on this machine

cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug assembleRelease \
  -PreactNativeArchitectures=arm64-v8a \
  --max-workers=2

adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk
```

Or: `npx expo run:android --device` when USB data works.

## GrapheneOS

- Prefer **Wireless debugging** (`adb pair` / `adb connect`) — USB file transfer is often blocked.
- Keep **dev** for coding and **prod** for daily use so icons stay distinct.

## Day-to-day JS

```bash
CI=0 EXPO_NO_TELEMETRY=1 npx expo start --dev-client --lan --port 8081
```

Open **dev** → `http://<laptop-wifi-ip>:8081` (same Wi‑Fi).

## EAS (optional)

`npx eas-cli build --platform android --profile development` (or `preview`) only if local SDK is unavailable. Free-plan quota applies. Not the default for routine rebuilds.
